# vegastack-mcp local dev secrets.
#
# v0.1 ships an anonymous public read MCP server with a per-IP rate limit
# (token-bucket, in-memory, per-isolate). v0.2 will move to per-tenant auth.
# Bearer-token auth is available now as an opt-in (REQUIRE_AUTH=true) for
# operators who want to gate their deployment.
#
# Copy to `.dev.vars` (NOT checked in) before `wrangler dev` if you need to
# override anything.

# Override the public CDN Registry pack base URL (defaults to vars.REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL)
# REGISTRY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://cli-registry.vegastack.com

# Override the cache TTL while iterating
# CACHE_TTL_SECONDS=60

# LOG_LEVEL=debug

# ── Rate limit (audit #77) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-IP requests-per-minute. Default 60. Buckets are keyed on
# cf-connecting-ip + colo and live in-memory in each Worker isolate.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=60

# ── Bearer-token auth (opt-in, audit #77) ────────────────────────────────
# Set REQUIRE_AUTH=true and provide MCP_AUTH_TOKEN to require every request
# to carry `Authorization: Bearer <MCP_AUTH_TOKEN>`. Comparison is
# constant-time. If REQUIRE_AUTH=true but MCP_AUTH_TOKEN is empty the
# server fails closed (500) — there is no silent-allow path.
#
# Generate a token with: `openssl rand -hex 32`
# Set in production via: `wrangler secret put MCP_AUTH_TOKEN`
# REQUIRE_AUTH=true
# MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-me-with-a-32-byte-hex-secret
